"OPEN DESIGN PROBLEM -- take conflicts: today two takes resolving in one round can BOTH succeed, the item hopping between inventories, the final owner being whoever happened to be processed last in the action system -- arbitrary, not a rule. Instant free-action takes sharpen this (first-committed wins by transaction order, which at least is a rule, but favors connection latency). Needs a deliberate resolution: contested-take rules (speed stat? opposed roll? both-fail-with-narration?), and the valuable flag above may be the lever that routes contested-worthy items through the slower, visible queue."